Subject: [PATCH] EXEC-MU-ACCOUNTS re-check round 2 (checker C2-TRACE): failing
 tests, two edge-bff services on one database

Two tests, kept in verification/edge_multiuser/access_tiers/pending/ until the two-site design is decided (outside
every suite, so CI stays green; pending/README.md names where they go back):
- a paid account's backtest queued on the switch-on site ends FAILED CAPABILITY_REQUIRED backtest.run when the
  switch-off site's queue loop claims it (principal.owner_principal applies the claiming service's switch);
- a start of the switch-off site copies its EDGE_PASSWORD_VERIFIER over user #1's password identity set on the
  switch-on site (accounts.py AccountStore.seed).

Both fail on ae9a1d8f at their asserted lines.

